### Register a new user
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": " Anna@Example.com ",
  "fullName": "Anna Smith",
  "password": "correct horse battery"
}

### Register the same email again (expect 409)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "anna@example.com",
  "fullName": "Anna Other",
  "password": "another long password"
}

### Register with broken fields (expect 400)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "fullName": "   ",
  "password": "short"
}

### Log in as Anna (expect 200 and an access token)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": " Anna@Example.com ",
  "password": "correct horse battery"
}

### Wrong password (expect 401 INVALID_CREDENTIALS)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "anna@example.com",
  "password": "wrong password here"
}

### Unknown email (expect the same 401)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nobody@example.com",
  "password": "wrong password here"
}

### Log in as Anna (expect 200 and an access token)
# @name login
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": " Anna@Example.com ",
  "password": "correct horse battery"
}

### Current user with the token (expect 200 and Anna)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Current user without a token (expect 401)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/me

